Subject: main: the entry point is pdEngineMain() on iOS

UIKit owns main() on iOS. app/ios/pd_ios_main.m is the real entry point: it
publishes the Documents/Caches paths, assembles argv and hands it to
SDL_UIKitRunApp(), which brings up UIApplication and then calls back into the
game on the main thread. The engine loop runs inside that call for the life of
the app, exactly as it does on the desktop.

Nothing else moves: with PLATFORM_IOS undefined this is upstream's main().

diff --git a/port/src/main.c b/port/src/main.c
index 2af38b9cb..fc8620c4d 100644
--- a/port/src/main.c
+++ b/port/src/main.c
@@ -196,7 +196,20 @@ static void mainApplySettingsRevision(void)
 	g_SettingsRevision = SETTINGS_REVISION;
 }
 
+#ifdef PLATFORM_IOS
+/**
+ * On iOS the process entry point belongs to UIKit, not to the game.
+ *
+ * app/ios/pd_ios_main.m owns main(), hands the argv to SDL_UIKitRunApp() and is
+ * called back here on the main thread once UIApplication is up. The engine's
+ * own loop then runs inside that call for the life of the app, exactly as it
+ * does on the desktop, and SDL's event pump is what keeps the UIKit run loop
+ * turning underneath it.
+ */
+int pdEngineMain(int argc, const char **argv)
+#else
 int main(int argc, const char **argv)
+#endif
 {
 	sysInitArgs(argc, argv);
 
